sts of virtual  connections on top of the physical layer  to achieve redundancy  we built redundancy across these layers  by having multiple routers and local  access points at  each physical network route and an  additional layer of redundancy with the  logical connections on top we even  leveraged google's private google access  to route all of uber's traffic to google  apis through the cloud interconnect vlan  attachments  this reduced the need of routing the  traffic through public internet and  provided additional reliability  to validate our architecture the teams  came up with a benchmarking suite that  validates all the physical and logical  network routes extensively and we find  any inefficiencies in this setup very  quickly this was extremely critical for  the success of the overall project  yeah i can i can only imagine how  connectivity and those benchmarking  tests must have been um so so critical  to to make this happen  now you've been on spanner for quite  some time how did the transition to  spanner help what were the benefits  you know priyanka building a specialized  database is extremely complex and  maintaining or operating it is much  harder with consistency as the primary  feature provided by spanner and it being  a managed solution we are able to  leverage a ton of storage  functionalities out of the box this has  given us time back to focus on building  the domain of fulfillment and providers  customers with richer experiences  so i cannot even imagine uh when you  were migrating to cloud spanner we were  still ordering food and rides how did  the team make sure that the migration  and switchover were seamless so the end  users could have the same experience  this was extremely tricky one of the  things that we agreed upon from the  beginning was an internal platform  re-architecture should not impact the  consumers in any way so we focused on  building the technology that would  seamlessly migrate any ongoing user  session from our old arc