 writes  wow awesome okay so what i heard is  networking optimization um caching and  also auto scaling  well awesome akit preetham thank you so  much for sharing such a complex system  design architecture and migration story  with cloud spanner as a star  i am absolutely blown away seeing what  it takes for my uber right to show up  reliably it was absolutely a pleasure  partnering with uber  on building the fulfillment platform  which is the backbone of uber's  architecture  and every time i take an uber i will get  to tell my kids that the ride was  powered by spanner thank you thank you  priyanka it was awesome to be here and  share our journey with spanner as a  building block and a redesign of our  application data models we have truly  laid the foundation for our next chapter  where we are working on scaling our  platform infrastructure by almost 10  times and building and modeling many  complex business features and verticals  on top  we are truly on day one of this journey  and there's a lot to do and explore  we're hiring come join us and be a part  of it well now you know what it will  take to scale and handle an application  with millions of concurrent requests  it's not magic it's google cloud spanner  and some planning did this help you let  me know in the comments below if you're  curious about any other use cases drop a  note and i will do my best to bring that  to you
 

